      "message": "This error is returned helpfully by Mesa when it fails to allocate memory. In the [latest upstream version](https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/blob/main/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_log.c#L293) it is a WARNING that would be caught by [1] but it seems that the version on the bots return an error incorrectly. Fixes could be to either:\n\n - Register the debug callback only when backend validation is enabled.\n - Use `instance` in this function to just LogCallbackData if the backend validation is not enabled.\n - (my slight preference) replace the assert with `DAWN_CHECK(!(messageTypes \u0026 VK_DEBUG_UTILS_MESSAGE_TYPE_VALIDATION_BIT_EXT))` to only crash on VVL messages.",
